312	    /** Move the claim to {@code next}; refused when the user's role may not open, settle or void it (see
313	     * {@link SettingsService#allowed}), and when its current status does not allow it (a PENDING
314	     * claim can only be voided here: it is approved or rejected instead). Settling it fixes what is due
315	     * on it as it shows then (what a statement bound it to, late charge included, when one did, otherwise its
316	     * person's rate then together with its late charge then, none on a correction); the user who opened it or last edited it
317	     * cannot settle it,
318	     * and a clerk's settle of it when that due is above the sheet's clerk limit (a due that is n/a is
319	     * within any limit) leaves it PENDING instead, fixing nothing, until a steward approves or rejects
320	     * it. A claim deferred on the sheet's today cannot be settled, nor one without proofs whose due is
321	     * above the proof threshold in force on its date (refused before the clerk limit is considered). A
322	     * SETTLED claim can only be voided by a steward, and only while the sheet's today is at most 7 days
323	     * after its settlement (its status log's SETTLED date); its frozen figure then leaves every total and
324	     * is recorded as reversed. A voided claim keeps its number, if it had one. An open of a claim whose due
325	 * is above the review threshold in force on its date leaves it in REVIEW instead, opened by the user but
326	 * with no number yet, until a steward reviews it (see {@link #review}); a REVIEW claim can only be voided
327	 * here. While the claim's person is flagged on the sheet's today, only a steward may open it. */
328	    @Transactional
329	    public Claim changeStatus(String sheetId, String user, long claimId, ClaimStatus next) {
330	        return changeStatus(sheetId, user, claimId, next, null);
331	    }
